WEBVTT

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:10.640
A song we do have the camera that rotates
around the focal point and we've set up the

00:00:10.641 --> 00:00:13.520
basis to the input
system to make this work.

00:00:13.521 --> 00:00:17.720
Now we need to rotate around that focal
point using the user input and we're going to

00:00:17.721 --> 00:00:20.240
use some rotation speed
to make that happen.

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:22.660
I want you to open
up your rotate camera

00:00:22.672 --> 00:00:25.120
script and we have the
awake method for finding

00:00:25.121 --> 00:00:28.800
the controls and enabling
what we needed to use.

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:30.909
Now we're going to
go down below or on a

00:00:30.921 --> 00:00:33.520
neighbour and we're going
to write another method

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.146
called void update and
make sure you have

00:00:36.158 --> 00:00:41.000
two curly braces below and that's
going to be able to help us check for it.

00:00:41.001 --> 00:00:43.569
So now we're going to want
to read the move action which

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:47.280
will be affected to as we've
done in previous videos.

00:00:47.281 --> 00:00:52.360
So we'll write a local variable which is a
vector to and we're going to call this move

00:00:52.361 --> 00:00:55.480
input because we only need
to use it in this method here.

00:00:55.481 --> 00:00:59.503
We'll set that equal to
the controls dot player

00:00:59.515 --> 00:01:04.720
dot move because now we found the
controls dot player and that's enabled.

00:01:04.721 --> 00:01:10.360
We can quite easily access the name move
within the script and then we'll say dot read

00:01:10.361 --> 00:01:14.440
value and in open and
close angled brackets.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:18.200
Then what I want you to do is write vector
two that we've done before and then at the

00:01:18.201 --> 00:01:21.920
end of that add the two parentheses and a
semicolon so we're going to make sure that

00:01:22.069 --> 00:01:27.360
we update the move input with the
value of whatever our move is at any point.

00:01:27.361 --> 00:01:29.800
So then we can begin to use this.

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:35.840
So we can then create another local variable
to store this and make it visually easier

00:01:35.889 --> 00:01:41.960
to understand so we can have a float called
horizontal input and then we can set that

00:01:44.129 --> 00:01:48.137
to move import dot x
because that is going to

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:52.080
be the thing that
moves us left and right or

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:58.520
using the A and D or the arrow
keys that we might want to use.

00:01:58.521 --> 00:02:03.200
Make sure you do add a semicolon to the end
just in case you forgot about it and then

00:02:03.201 --> 00:02:05.525
below here then we
need to use this in our

00:02:05.537 --> 00:02:08.039
transform dot rotate to
make sure that we can

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.508
use the horizontal input.
We can say transform

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:16.520
dot rotate with a capital
R is going to rotate

00:02:16.521 --> 00:02:22.271
around something and then
we're going to say vector three dot

00:02:22.272 --> 00:02:26.360
up add a comma and then we're
going to use our horizontal input.

00:02:26.361 --> 00:02:28.783
Of course we could
use move input dot x but

00:02:28.795 --> 00:02:31.400
sometimes giving it an
M like horizontal input

00:02:31.401 --> 00:02:36.000
makes it easy to understand if you're looking
back and then we're going to times by a

00:02:36.001 --> 00:02:42.240
rotation speed which we haven't quite created
and then we'll also multiply by time dot

00:02:42.315 --> 00:02:47.320
delta time and end the bracket and the
semicolon just so that we can make sure this

00:02:47.321 --> 00:02:51.520
is done frame rate independent
and across a period of time.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:55.520
I want to head to the top of our script and
have a public variable and we're going to

00:02:55.570 --> 00:03:01.840
have this as a float and call this rotation
speed like we wanted so that equal we could

00:03:01.841 --> 00:03:05.655
say 150 F just for now
and you can make sure

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:09.320
